          "question": "I have had reflux for years and now food sometimes sticks going down. How worrying is that, and what does guidance describe about when to investigate?",
          "answer": "Food sticking while swallowing can be related to conditions affecting the esophagus, including reflux disease. It’s important to discuss your symptoms with a healthcare professional, as they can evaluate your condition in person.\n\nAccording to the guidance, you should seek further investigation if you experience any of the following: \n\n1. *Difficulty swallowing* (dysphagia) that persists.\n2. *Pain* while swallowing.\n3. *Unexplained weight loss*.\n4. *Vomiting* blood or having black stools.\n5. *New onset of dysphagia* in individuals over 50, or changes in swallowing ability.\n\nThese signs may indicate complications or other conditions requiring attention. \n\nI did not cover specific treatment options, detailed diagnostic procedures, or any potential underlying causes. Please consult a clinician for a thorough evaluation and personalized advice.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
